LightCraft is an open source photo library and raw developer, a
clean-room reimplementation of the Adobe Lightroom workflow written in
pure Rust by the ArtCraft team.  It imports, rates, keywords and
organizes photos, and develops raw files non-destructively with
exposure, tone curves, color grading, local masks and presets, processed
on the GPU through wgpu.  Denoising, face recognition and AI masks use
models that are downloaded on request.

The lightcraft-cli tool renders and runs the same engine commands from
scripts, and serves them over MCP for agents.
